# ============================================================================
# SoyMutDB public portal (apps/web) — Cloudflare Pages custom headers
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# GitHub Pages does NOT read this file. The gh-pages demo therefore serves no
# custom headers at all; that gap is documented in
# docs/ops/static-hosting-security.md and is one of the reasons Cloudflare Pages
# is the production static host.
#
# Rules match per request path and a request inherits headers from ALL matching
# rules, with duplicate headers comma-joined. `/*` below therefore deliberately
# carries NO Cache-Control: it would merge with the /assets/* rule.
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security headers — every response.
#
# HSTS carries no `includeSubDomains` and no `preload`: sibling staging and API
# subdomains are not all Cloudflare-fronted, and pinning them would make the
# browser refuse to connect over plain HTTP to hosts this project does not
# control. (Same reasoning as apps/admin/public/_headers.)
#
# There is no Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy here on purpose. It is not required by
# any finding, and severing the browsing-context group breaks
# `window.opener`-based flows (popup sign-in, payment windows) in ways that only
# show up in a browser. It would need its own tested change, not a drive-by
# addition to a header block.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; frame-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; object-src 'none'; worker-src 'self' blob:

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hashed build assets — Vite emits /assets/<name>-<hash>.<ext>.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HTML documents — always revalidate.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# ============================================================================
# BUILD-TIME REPLACEMENT — do not hand-edit the CSP above
#
# `apps/web/scripts/finalize-csp.ts` rewrites the CSP line on every build, after
# every HTML-producing step and before gzip/gen-sw/manifest, using the same
# `buildCsp()` the pages' <meta> policies are generated from. It substitutes:
#
#   * connect-src 'self' <the API origin the build was configured with>
#   * frame-src   'self' <the JBrowse origin the build was configured with>
#                        (omitted in minimal mode)
#   * script-src  <per-page sha256 hashes of inline scripts>, with
#     'unsafe-inline' REMOVED    (see apps/web/scripts/finalize-csp.ts)
#
# The policy above is the conservative pre-finalization default: same-origin
# only, no placeholder origin. It is a REAL policy rather than a sentinel token
# so that a partial build (for example `build:ui`, which runs only
# `vite build`) publishes a narrower working policy instead of an invalid header
# or an empty one. A cross-origin deployment built that way fails loudly at
# runtime, and scripts/check_artifact_headers.py fails the build that produced
# it, because the finalized policy must carry the configured origin AND the
# inline-script hashes, and must no longer equal this default.
# ============================================================================
